# The QEMU every guest in CI runs, and the one the dev host runs.
#
# One declaration, read by `ci.yml`'s twelve shards, by `tcg`, by `gate-a.yml`
# and by the build system's own prerequisite check. `specs/ci-plan.md` §7.3 is
# why it is worth a file: on one runner image, one commit and one accelerator,
# `desktop_typing_damage` is red on QEMU 8.2.2 and green on 11.0.3, and
# `usb_storage_shapes` with it. The version is a variable that decides test
# outcomes, and `debian:sid` is a rolling release, so leaving it undeclared
# means the instrument can move out from under every recorded measurement
# without anything saying so.
#
# Changing this line is a deliberate act: it says the instrument moved and that
# every number taken before it was taken on a different one.
11.0.3
